   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "There is / there are",
     "texto": [
      "«There is/are» is **es gibt**, and it works for singular and plural. What there is goes in the **accusative**: **Es gibt einen Garten** (there is a garden), **Es gibt eine Küche**, **Es gibt ein Bad**.",
      "In the negative, with **kein**: **Es gibt keinen Garten** (there is no garden).",
      "In questions, the verb comes first: **Gibt es einen Garten?**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Es gibt",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Masculine",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Feminine",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Neuter",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
